-- One source (Avik, 2026-11-15: "ONE SOURCE OF INFORMATION"; "Nothing is ever allowed to be stale";
-- "by construction we must ensure no pushes violate this"): no rendered presentation is stored
-- (.pdf, .docx, .epub: a presentation is computed from the value it presents); no line of prose of
-- 100 characters or more is held by two files (whitespace and leading > set aside; of a .cub file
-- outside the code, the text inside its string literals, the paper's lines). Code (src/, lib/,
-- experiments/, tests/, playground/) is not prose. A file is read as git stages it: its size and
-- modification time must be the ones the index recorded, else it is refused until staged whole.
os-lower : Word → Word
os-lower b = if andB (wlt #64 b) (wlt b #91) then wadd b #32 else b
